  "Usage: sh [-i] [-c SOURCE [NAME [ARG...]] | -s [ARG...] | FILE [ARG...]]\n  -c SOURCE   execute shell source\n  -s          read commands from standard input\n  -i          enable a persistent line-oriented interactive session\n  --help      display this help and exit\n  --version   display version and exit\nSupports arithmetic assignment, backticks, expanded here-documents, stdout/stderr copies, loop control and printf/test builtins.\nTerminal job control, descriptor import/closure and complete POSIX/Bash grammar remain unavailable.\nShell test -s follows target metadata; unavailable target sizes are rejected.\nMalformed shell command lists reject before execution; complete EOF continuations execute.\nOn POSIX, every file-test operand ending in a slash must name a directory.\n"
